# Proposed (milestone2.md, "BallVector": bv_mul_pow2_k): the one radius of a BallVector times a positive
# power of two c, the radius lines of ball_mul_pow2_k with the exactness of the centers over all
# entries (ex, the and of the step's masks): c rx when every center was scaled exactly and so was the
# radius, otherwise the second number after RN(c rx), at least c rx + eta (eta covers what one center
# lost); an infinite center (an overflow, m infinite) carried into the radius as a NaN (m - m), so
# that the finish norm_finish_1 gives the whole space. Its claim is not in the vocabulary: "rz >= c rx,
# and rz >= c rx + eta when ex or the radius's exactness is false, and rz = c rx otherwise" needs an
# upper bound under the negation of a mask input (bv_proposals.py checks it).
kernel:        bv_mul_pow2_radius
input:         stored m
input:         mask ex
input:         stored rx
input:         c
output:        rz
status:        unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the radius is selected and stepped, as in ball_mul_pow2_k; an infinite center reaches it through m - m, and the finish tests it

rr = prod(rx, c)
br = lt(const up(eta/(2*u)), rr)
zr = eq(rx, 0)
er = or(br, zr)
q  = and(ex, er)
su = succ(rr)
rw = succ(su)
rs = select(q, rr, rw)
d  = sub(m, m)
rz = add(rs, d)
